{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And Avraham weighed to Ephron.</b> Defective — missing a vav; for he said 'much,' yet even a little he did not do (Bava Metzia 7) — he took from him large shekels, which are kantarin, as it says ״current with the merchant״ — accepted by weight everywhere (there and Bekhorot 50); and there is a place whose shekels are large, which are kantarin, צנטינא\"רש בְּלַעַ\"ז."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The la'az צנטינא\"רש appears to correspond to Old French centeniers or a related form denoting a weight/coin; Rashi cites it as the vernacular equivalent of קַנְטָרִין."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:06.233737002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}